  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 145 PM CST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nMonday Night through Wednesday\nAssessment...high (>80%) confidence on a storm system bringing\nsome rain to the area along with warmer than normal temperatures.\n\nAlthough there are differences between the global models, they have \nbeen consistent in taking the center of the significant system well \nto the west of the area. The net result will be much warmer than \nnormal temperatures for the area along with windy conditions. \nPeriodic rounds of rain will be seen with the best chances being \nMonday night into Tuesday.\n\nThe overall timing for the best chances for rain also agrees with \nthe surge of moisture from the Pacific along with some from the \nGulf. The model PWATs with the moisture surge are 1.5+ inches which \nwould exceed the local sounding climatology. Such moisture also \nyields a high probability of locally heavy rainfall, especially with \nany thunderstorms.\n\nThunderstorms will be possible since we'll be in the warm sector of \nthe storm. The main severe risk on Monday/Monday night looks to\nhold off to the southwest of our area, but SPC's latest update \ndid push the Marginal Risk (level 1 or 5) northeastward to \ninclude portions of far NE Missouri. Isolated damaging winds \nappear to be the primary threat.\n\nOnce the main cold front and a secondary low sweep through the \narea on Wednesday, spotty showers and sprinkles will be possible\nthe second half of the work week.\n\nTemperatures will cool down by the middle to end of the week \nbut still average above normal for early November.",
